===Students' Union===
Students at the university are represented by the Students' Union (HopeSU), which is affiliated to the [[National Union of Students (United Kingdom)|National Union of Students]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.hopesu.com|title=HopeSU|access-date=25 August 2020}}</ref>

===Student body===

In {{HESA year}} the university had {{HESA student population|INSTID=0023}} students including {{HESA undergraduate population|INSTID=0023}} undergraduates and {{HESA postgraduate population|INSTID=0023}} postgraduates, making it the [[List of universities in the United Kingdom by enrollment|{{HESA student population rank|INSTID=0023}} largest]] university in the UK (out of the {{HESA total}} universities included in [[Higher Education Statistics Agency|HESA]] statistics).<ref name="HESA citation"/> The university is less than half the size of the other two universities in the Liverpool metropolitan area with comparable histories, [[Edge Hill University|Edge Hill]] ({{HESA student population|INSTID=0016}} students) and its elder sister [[University of Chester|Chester]] ({{HESA student population|INSTID=0011}} students).<ref name="HESA citation"/>

The university has a greater number and proportion of postgraduates than four of the six universities closest to it in size.<ref name="HESA citation"/>
